summary: usex UNIX System Exerciser test
description: |
  The usex UNIX System Exerciser gives its user the capability of thoroughly exercising and testing several different kernel subsystems.
  Usex is a single executable that acts as as test harness controlling one or more test programs.
contact: Fendy Tjahjadi <ftjahjad@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
id: e1807ae2-7de1-47b1-9717-b488ac7709e7
tag:
  - KT1-9
  - KernelTier1
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - ncurses-devel
  - make
  - gcc
  - glibc-static
  - glibc-kernheaders
  - restraint-rhts
extra-summary: standards/usex
extra-task: standards/usex
enabled: true
duration: 60m
adjust+:
  - when: arch == s390x
    enabled: false
